From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:01:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] state: online FTS plan refuses what it cannot attribute;
 one-shot rebuild never drops a shared tree [daveey]

Review round 2 of the online FTS recovery:
- plan_from_check: a Tree line whose root this snapshot cannot name (including Tree 1, the schema)
  refuses; a check at its error limit refuses (walk incomplete); schema and check come from one
  read snapshot; FTS5 xIntegrity blob lines no longer unlink (page structure sound: drained, file
  ends clean); family_of full-matches the FTS5 shadow suffixes.
- recover_stale_fts_online re-checks a peer's recovery and the index root pages under the rebuild
  authority (the plan ran without it); a refused plan is not repeated by the automatic retry for
  6 h (a whole-file check of a large store).
- _recover_stale_fts_locked (existing one-shot) now asks the same plan first. On the hub's damage
  shape its DROP succeeded and freed the shared page twice; the reviewer showed the page then
  reaches canonical data after ordinary inserts. A named family skips the DROP and the retry
  recovers online; a refused plan skips it and points at `hermes sessions recover`.

Tests: plan attribution table (Tree 1, unmapped root, canonical tree, freelist, limit); FTS5-only
lines drain; full-match names; a page shared with `messages` is never drained; the one-shot at
open steps aside on the hub shape and the retry recovers with no double reference left.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
